§ `The dates module`

#ASSERT `the 30 Nov 2025 plus 3 months` EQUALS `28 Feb 2026`
#ASSERT (`15 Jan 2026` `plus calendar months` 4) EQUALS `15 May 2026`
#ASSERT (`1 Jun 2026` `plus days` 42) EQUALS `13 Jul 2026`
#ASSERT `14 Apr 2026` `is on or before` `14 Apr 2026`
#ASSERT (NOT (`15 Apr 2026` `is on or before` `14 Apr 2026`))

`the 30 Nov 2025 plus 3 months` MEANS `30 Nov 2025` `plus calendar months` 3

§ `s 251B -- authorisation`

-- A traditional process exists and was followed: authorised. Exists and not followed (an agreed process used instead):
-- not authorised. No traditional process, agreed process used: authorised.
#ASSERT `s 251B -- the applicant is authorised by all the persons in the group` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 251B -- the applicant is authorised by all the persons in the group` TRUE FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT `s 251B -- the applicant is authorised by all the persons in the group` FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 251B -- the applicant is authorised by all the persons in the group` FALSE FALSE FALSE))

§ `s 61 with s 61A -- can we make a native title determination application`

-- Order of inputs: in group; traditional process must be followed; authorised by it; authorised by agreed process;
-- approved determination; previous exclusive possession act; previous non-exclusive possession act; exclusive claimed
-- over it; ss 47-47C disregard and the application says so.

-- C1 everything in order, no previous acts: yes.
#ASSERT `s 61 -- can we make a native title determination application` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the person or persons the group authorised may apply to the Federal Court, and will jointly be the applicant (s 61(1), (2)); the application must meet ss 61(3)-(5) and 62`
-- C2 the person is not in the group, though authorised: no.
#ASSERT `s 61 -- can we make a native title determination application` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the person who applies must also be included in the native title claim group (s 61(1), the text's no)`
-- C3 traditional process exists but the meeting used a majority vote instead: not authorised.
#ASSERT `s 61 -- can we make a native title determination application` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the applicant must be authorised by all the persons in the native title claim group, in the way s 251B requires (s 61(1), s 251B, the text's no)`
-- C4 approved determination over the area: no, under s 61A(1), even if ss 47-47C would apply.
#ASSERT `s 61 -- can we make a native title determination application` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: s 61A forbids this application` `no: there is an approved determination of native title for the area (s 61A(1), the text's no)`
-- C5 freehold grant (previous exclusive possession act) over part: no under s 61A(2).
#ASSERT `s 61 -- can we make a native title determination application` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 61A forbids this application` `no: it must not cover any of an area where a previous exclusive possession act was done (s 61A(2), the text's no); leave that area out, or, if ss 47, 47A, 47B or 47C require that extinguishment to be disregarded, say so in the application (s 61A(4))`
-- C6 the same, but s 47A disregards it and the application says so: yes (s 61A(4)).
#ASSERT `s 61 -- can we make a native title determination application` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the person or persons the group authorised may apply to the Federal Court, and will jointly be the applicant (s 61(1), (2)); the application must meet ss 61(3)-(5) and 62`
-- C7 pastoral lease (non-exclusive) and exclusive possession claimed over it: not as framed.
#ASSERT `s 61 -- can we make a native title determination application` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 61A forbids this application` `not as framed: it must not claim possession, occupation, use and enjoyment to the exclusion of all others over an area where a previous non-exclusive possession act was done (s 61A(3), the text's no); claim non-exclusive rights there, or rely on ss 47-47C and say so (s 61A(4))`
-- C8 pastoral lease, only non-exclusive rights claimed there: yes.
#ASSERT `s 61 -- can we make a native title determination application` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the person or persons the group authorised may apply to the Federal Court, and will jointly be the applicant (s 61(1), (2)); the application must meet ss 61(3)-(5) and 62`
-- C9 the s 61A helper alone: exclusive claimed with no previous non-exclusive possession act is not a s 61A(3) problem.
#ASSERT `s 61A -- what it says about our application` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 61A does not stop it`

§ `ss 47, 47A, 47B -- earlier extinguishment disregarded`

-- Order: pastoral lease held by claimants; area held for Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander peoples; vacant Crown land;
-- a member occupies.
#ASSERT `ss 47-47B -- is earlier extinguishment disregarded` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes, under s 47: the extinguishment by the pastoral lease, any other interest, and acts under it is disregarded for all purposes of the application (s 47(2)); you must still show connection`
#ASSERT `ss 47-47B -- is earlier extinguishment disregarded` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes, under s 47A: the extinguishment by the grant, vesting, holding or reservation for Aboriginal peoples or Torres Strait Islanders, and by other prior interests, is disregarded (s 47A(2)); you must still show connection`
-- Aboriginal reserve, but nobody in the group occupies it: s 47A does not apply.
#ASSERT `ss 47-47B -- is earlier extinguishment disregarded` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not under ss 47, 47A or 47B on these facts: each applies only if its conditions hold (the text's no); s 47C (park areas, by agreement) is not encoded here`
#ASSERT `ss 47-47B -- is earlier extinguishment disregarded` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes, under s 47B: the extinguishment by the creation of any prior interest in this vacant Crown land is disregarded (s 47B(2)); you must still show connection`
#ASSERT `ss 47-47B -- is earlier extinguishment disregarded` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not under ss 47, 47A or 47B on these facts: each applies only if its conditions hold (the text's no); s 47C (park areas, by agreement) is not encoded here`
#ASSERT `ss 47-47B -- is earlier extinguishment disregarded` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not under ss 47, 47A or 47B on these facts: each applies only if its conditions hold (the text's no); s 47C (park areas, by agreement) is not encoded here`

§ `ss 190A-190C -- registration`

-- Order: amended; earlier accepted; amendment only minor; 190B(2); (3); (4); (5); (6); (7); 61A forbade (8);
-- minerals (9)(a); offshore (9)(b); otherwise extinguished (9)(c); 190C(2); overlapping group (3); certified (4)(a);
-- member authorised (4AA)(a); conditions satisfied (4AA)(b); statements and grounds (5).

-- R1 an original, certified claim meeting every condition: accepted under s 190A(6).
#ASSERT `ss 190A-190C -- will our claim be registered` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Registrar must accept the claim, as it meets every condition in ss 190B and 190C (s 190A(6))`
-- R2 uncertified, but the applicant is an authorised member, no conditions, and the application says so with grounds.
#ASSERT `ss 190A-190C -- will our claim be registered` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the Registrar must accept the claim, as it meets every condition in ss 190B and 190C (s 190A(6))`
-- R3 the same, but the application does not state the authorisation and grounds: s 190C(4) fails (s 190C(5)).
#ASSERT `ss 190A-190C -- will our claim be registered` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: the Registrar must not accept the claim (s 190A(6B), the text's no); you will be given reasons (s 190D) and may seek reconsideration by the NNTT (s 190E) or review by the Federal Court (s 190F)` (LIST "s 190C(4): neither certified by every representative body nor shown to be authorised by all the group")
-- R4 only physical connection fails.
#ASSERT `ss 190A-190C -- will our claim be registered` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the Registrar must not accept the claim (s 190A(6B), the text's no); you will be given reasons (s 190D) and may seek reconsideration by the NNTT (s 190E) or review by the Federal Court (s 190F)` (LIST "s 190B(7): no traditional physical connection shown")
-- R5 three failures, listed in the Act's order: factual basis, minerals, overlapping group.
#ASSERT `ss 190A-190C -- will our claim be registered` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the Registrar must not accept the claim (s 190A(6B), the text's no); you will be given reasons (s 190D) and may seek reconsideration by the NNTT (s 190E) or review by the Federal Court (s 190F)` (LIST "s 190B(5): factual basis not sufficient", "s 190B(9)(a): minerals, petroleum or gas claimed are wholly owned by the Crown", "s 190C(3): a member was in an earlier registered overlapping claim group")
-- R6 an amended claim that only reduces the area, after the earlier claim was accepted: accepted under s 190A(6A), even
-- though the inputs for s 190B(5) say no (the Registrar does not test it again).
#ASSERT `ss 190A-190C -- will our claim be registered` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Registrar must accept the amended claim, since the earlier claim was accepted and the amendment only does one of the things s 190A(6A) lists`
-- R7 an amended claim that changes more (adds an area): tested again under s 190A(6) and passes.
#ASSERT `ss 190A-190C -- will our claim be registered` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Registrar must accept the claim, as it meets every condition in ss 190B and 190C (s 190A(6))`
-- R8 s 61A forbade it and the rights were extinguished: two failures.
#ASSERT `ss 190A-190C -- will our claim be registered` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the Registrar must not accept the claim (s 190A(6B), the text's no); you will be given reasons (s 190D) and may seek reconsideration by the NNTT (s 190E) or review by the Federal Court (s 190F)` (LIST "s 190B(8): s 61A forbade the application", "s 190B(9)(c): rights claimed otherwise extinguished")

§ `s 190A(2) -- when should the Registrar finish`

-- s 29 notice, notification day 15 January 2026: 4 months after is 15 May 2026.
#ASSERT `s 190A(2) -- when should the Registrar finish` TRUE `15 Jan 2026` FALSE `15 Jan 2026` EQUALS `by the end of this day, on best endeavours (s 190A(2))` `15 May 2026`
-- s 24MD(6B)(c) notification given 1 April 2026: 2 months after is 1 June 2026.
#ASSERT `s 190A(2) -- when should the Registrar finish` FALSE `15 Jan 2026` TRUE `1 Apr 2026` EQUALS `by the end of this day, on best endeavours (s 190A(2))` `1 Jun 2026`
-- Both: the earlier, 15 May 2026 (s 29) before 1 June 2026.
#ASSERT `s 190A(2) -- when should the Registrar finish` TRUE `15 Jan 2026` TRUE `1 Apr 2026` EQUALS `by the end of this day, on best endeavours (s 190A(2))` `15 May 2026`
-- Both, the s 24MD one earlier: given 1 March 2026, 2 months on is 1 May 2026, before 15 May 2026.
#ASSERT `s 190A(2) -- when should the Registrar finish` TRUE `15 Jan 2026` TRUE `1 Mar 2026` EQUALS `by the end of this day, on best endeavours (s 190A(2))` `1 May 2026`
-- Month end: notification day 31 October 2025, 4 months on has no 31 February: 28 February 2026.
#ASSERT `s 190A(2) -- when should the Registrar finish` TRUE `31 Oct 2025` FALSE `15 Jan 2026` EQUALS `by the end of this day, on best endeavours (s 190A(2))` `28 Feb 2026`
-- Neither: as soon as practicable.
#ASSERT `s 190A(2) -- when should the Registrar finish` FALSE `15 Jan 2026` FALSE `15 Jan 2026` EQUALS `as soon as is practicable; the Act sets no day (s 190A(2A))`

§ `s 190E -- reconsideration by the NNTT`

-- Notice given 1 June 2026: 42 days after is 13 July 2026 (29 days to 30 June, 13 more).
#ASSERT `s 190E(2)(b) -- the last day to apply for reconsideration` `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `13 Jul 2026`
-- Applying on the last day: in time.
#ASSERT `s 190E -- can I apply for reconsideration` TRUE `1 Jun 2026` FALSE FALSE `13 Jul 2026` EQUALS `yes, in time: apply in writing, stating the basis on which reconsideration is sought (s 190E(1), (2))`
-- One day late.
#ASSERT `s 190E -- can I apply for reconsideration` TRUE `1 Jun 2026` FALSE FALSE `14 Jul 2026` EQUALS `no: out of time, more than 42 days after the notice was given (s 190E(2)(b), the text's no); review by the Federal Court remains (s 190F)`
-- On the day of the notice: in time.
#ASSERT `s 190E -- can I apply for reconsideration` TRUE `1 Jun 2026` FALSE FALSE `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `yes, in time: apply in writing, stating the basis on which reconsideration is sought (s 190E(1), (2))`
-- No notice of refusal yet.
#ASSERT `s 190E -- can I apply for reconsideration` FALSE `1 Jun 2026` FALSE FALSE `13 Jul 2026` EQUALS `no: reconsideration is available only after the Registrar gives notice under s 190D(1) of a decision not to accept the claim (s 190E(1), the text's no)`
-- Already went to the Federal Court.
#ASSERT `s 190E -- can I apply for reconsideration` TRUE `1 Jun 2026` TRUE FALSE `15 Jul 2026` EQUALS `no: you have already applied to the Federal Court for review under s 190F(1) (s 190E(3), the text's no)`
-- A second reconsideration, though in time.
#ASSERT `s 190E -- can I apply for reconsideration` TRUE `1 Jun 2026` FALSE TRUE `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `no: you may apply to the NNTT for reconsideration no more than once (s 190E(4), the text's no)`

§ `s 190F -- review by the Federal Court`

#ASSERT `s 190F -- can I seek review by the Federal Court` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: you may apply for review of the Registrar's decision (s 190F(1)); the Act sets no time limit`
#ASSERT `s 190F -- can I seek review by the Federal Court` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not now: you cannot apply while the NNTT is reconsidering the claim under s 190E (s 190F(1), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 190F -- can I seek review by the Federal Court` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: review is available only after the Registrar gives notice under s 190D(1) of a decision not to accept the claim (s 190F(1), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 190F -- can I seek review by the Federal Court` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: you may apply for review; as the only reason for refusal was physical connection, the Court may order the Registrar to accept the claim, since it is satisfied of s 190F(3)(a) and (b)`
-- Physical connection the only failure, but the Court is not satisfied of the parent's connection: review only.
#ASSERT `s 190F -- can I seek review by the Federal Court` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: you may apply for review of the Registrar's decision (s 190F(1)); the Act sets no time limit`

§ `ss 66, 84 -- becoming a party`

-- Notification day 15 January 2026: the period of 3 months starting on that day ends on 14 April 2026.
#ASSERT `s 66(10)(c) -- the last day to notify the Federal Court` `15 Jan 2026` EQUALS `14 Apr 2026`
-- Month end: starting 30 November 2025, 3 months on is 28 February 2026, so the last day is 27 February 2026.
#ASSERT `s 66(10)(c) -- the last day to notify the Federal Court` `30 Nov 2025` EQUALS `27 Feb 2026`
-- Order: applicant; claim native title; registered claimant or body corporate; interest affected; notification day;
-- notified; notified on; joined; today.
-- P1 the applicant.
#ASSERT `ss 66, 84 -- am I a party` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `15 Jan 2026` FALSE `15 Jan 2026` FALSE `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `yes: the applicant is a party (s 84(2))`
-- P2 a member of a neighbouring group claiming native title in the area, notified on the last day.
#ASSERT `ss 66, 84 -- am I a party` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `15 Jan 2026` TRUE `14 Apr 2026` FALSE `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `yes: you notified the Federal Court in time, and you are a person s 84(3)(a) covers (s 84(3))`
-- P3 the same, notified a day late.
#ASSERT `ss 66, 84 -- am I a party` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `15 Jan 2026` TRUE `15 Apr 2026` FALSE `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `no: the period of 3 months starting on the notification day has ended (ss 66(10)(c), 84(3)(b), the text's no); the Court may still join you if satisfied your interests may be affected and it is in the interests of justice (s 84(5))`
-- P4 the same, late but joined by the Court.
#ASSERT `ss 66, 84 -- am I a party` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `15 Jan 2026` TRUE `15 Apr 2026` TRUE `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `yes: the Federal Court has joined you as a party (s 84(5))`
-- P5 not yet notified, today 1 April 2026: notify by 14 April 2026.
#ASSERT `ss 66, 84 -- am I a party` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `15 Jan 2026` FALSE `15 Jan 2026` FALSE `1 Apr 2026` EQUALS `not yet: notify the Federal Court in writing by the last day` `14 Apr 2026`
-- P6 not yet notified, today 14 April 2026 (the last day): still not yet.
#ASSERT `ss 66, 84 -- am I a party` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `15 Jan 2026` FALSE `15 Jan 2026` FALSE `14 Apr 2026` EQUALS `not yet: notify the Federal Court in writing by the last day` `14 Apr 2026`
-- P7 not yet notified, today 15 April 2026: the period has ended.
#ASSERT `ss 66, 84 -- am I a party` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `15 Jan 2026` FALSE `15 Jan 2026` FALSE `15 Apr 2026` EQUALS `no: the period of 3 months starting on the notification day has ended (ss 66(10)(c), 84(3)(b), the text's no); the Court may still join you if satisfied your interests may be affected and it is in the interests of justice (s 84(5))`
-- P8 no claim, no registration, no interest affected: not under s 84(3), even if notified in time.
#ASSERT `ss 66, 84 -- am I a party` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `15 Jan 2026` TRUE `1 Apr 2026` FALSE `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `not under s 84(3): you are not a person it covers (the text's no); the Court may still join you if satisfied your interests may be affected and it is in the interests of justice (s 84(5))`
-- P9 a registered native title claimant for an overlapping area, notified on the notification day itself.
#ASSERT `ss 66, 84 -- am I a party` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `15 Jan 2026` TRUE `15 Jan 2026` FALSE `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `yes: you notified the Federal Court in time, and you are a person s 84(3)(a) covers (s 84(3))`

§ `s 66B -- replacing the applicant`

-- Order: member; consents; no longer authorised; exceeded authority; died or cannot act; we are authorised.
#ASSERT `s 66B -- can I apply to replace the applicant` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes, under s 66B(1): you may apply to replace the applicant; the Court may order it if satisfied the grounds are established (s 66B(2))`
#ASSERT `s 66B -- can I apply to replace the applicant` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: you (the members applying) must be authorised by the claim group to make the application and deal with matters arising (s 66B(1)(b), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 66B -- can I apply to replace the applicant` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: none of the s 66B(1)(a) grounds applies to the current applicant (consent, no longer authorised, exceeded authority), and no one has died or become incapable (the text's no)`
-- One of the joint applicants has died; the applying member need not yet be authorised to apply (s 66B(2A)).
#ASSERT `s 66B -- can I apply to replace the applicant` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes, under s 66B(2A): a member of the group may apply because a person who is the applicant has died or cannot act; the Court may order replacement as s 66B(2B) allows`
#ASSERT `s 66B -- can I apply to replace the applicant` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: only a member of the claim group may apply (s 66B(1), (2A), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 66B -- can I apply to replace the applicant` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes, under s 66B(1): you may apply to replace the applicant; the Court may order it if satisfied the grounds are established (s 66B(2))`
#ASSERT `s 66B -- can I apply to replace the applicant` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes, under s 66B(1): you may apply to replace the applicant; the Court may order it if satisfied the grounds are established (s 66B(2))`

§ `ss 29, 30 -- native title party`

-- Notification day 15 January 2026: file by 15 April 2026, registered by 15 May 2026.
#ASSERT `s 30(1)(a) -- the last day to file and the day to be registered by` `15 Jan 2026` EQUALS LIST `15 Apr 2026`, `15 May 2026`
-- Month end: notification day 30 November 2025: file by 28 February 2026, registered by 30 March 2026.
#ASSERT `s 30(1)(a) -- the last day to file and the day to be registered by` `30 Nov 2025` EQUALS LIST `28 Feb 2026`, `30 Mar 2026`
-- Order: relates; notification day; registered at notice; body corporate covers all; filed on; entered; entered on;
-- still on Register; today.
-- N1 already registered when notice was given: native title party under s 29(2)(b)(i).
#ASSERT `ss 29, 30 -- are we a native title party` TRUE `15 Jan 2026` TRUE FALSE `1 Mar 2026` TRUE `1 Mar 2026` TRUE `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `yes: you were a registered native title claimant for the affected area when notice was given, so you are a native title party (s 29(2)(b)(i))`
-- N2 filed on the last day (15 April 2026) and registered on the last day (15 May 2026): s 30(1)(a).
#ASSERT `ss 29, 30 -- are we a native title party` TRUE `15 Jan 2026` FALSE FALSE `15 Apr 2026` TRUE `15 May 2026` TRUE `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `yes: the application was filed in time and the claim was on the Register 4 months after the notification day (s 30(1)(a))`
-- N3 filed a day late (16 April 2026), registered in time: no.
#ASSERT `ss 29, 30 -- are we a native title party` TRUE `15 Jan 2026` FALSE FALSE `16 Apr 2026` TRUE `1 May 2026` TRUE `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `no: the application was not filed before the end of 3 months after the notification day (s 30(1)(a)(i), the text's no)`
-- N4 filed in time, registered a day late (16 May 2026): no.
#ASSERT `ss 29, 30 -- are we a native title party` TRUE `15 Jan 2026` FALSE FALSE `1 Apr 2026` TRUE `16 May 2026` TRUE `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `no: the claim was not on the Register 4 months after the notification day (s 30(1)(a), the text's no)`
-- N5 filed in time, not yet registered, today 1 May 2026: not yet, by 15 May 2026.
#ASSERT `ss 29, 30 -- are we a native title party` TRUE `15 Jan 2026` FALSE FALSE `1 Apr 2026` FALSE `1 Jan 2026` TRUE `1 May 2026` EQUALS `not yet: the application was filed in time; you will be a native title party if the claim is on the Register by this day` `15 May 2026`
-- N6 filed in time, not registered, today 16 May 2026: no.
#ASSERT `ss 29, 30 -- are we a native title party` TRUE `15 Jan 2026` FALSE FALSE `1 Apr 2026` FALSE `1 Jan 2026` TRUE `16 May 2026` EQUALS `no: the claim was not on the Register 4 months after the notification day (s 30(1)(a), the text's no)`
-- N7 registered, then removed from the Register: ceased (s 30(2)).
#ASSERT `ss 29, 30 -- are we a native title party` TRUE `15 Jan 2026` TRUE FALSE `1 Mar 2025` TRUE `1 Jun 2025` FALSE `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `no: you have ceased to be a registered native title claimant, so you have ceased to be a native title party (s 30(2), the text's no)`
-- N8 the claim does not touch the affected land.
#ASSERT `ss 29, 30 -- are we a native title party` FALSE `15 Jan 2026` TRUE FALSE `1 Mar 2025` TRUE `1 Jun 2025` TRUE `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `no: the claim does not relate to any of the land or waters the act will affect (ss 29(2), 30(1)(a)(ii), the text's no)`
-- N9 registered at notice, but bodies corporate cover all the land (no s 29 notice to claimants); the application was
-- filed before the notification day and the claim was on the Register: still a party under s 30(1)(a) (finding 4).
#ASSERT `ss 29, 30 -- are we a native title party` TRUE `15 Jan 2026` TRUE TRUE `1 Mar 2025` TRUE `1 Jun 2025` TRUE `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `yes: the application was filed in time and the claim was on the Register 4 months after the notification day (s 30(1)(a))`

§ `s 32 -- the expedited procedure`

#ASSERT `s 32(3) -- the last day to object` `15 Jan 2026` EQUALS `15 May 2026`
#ASSERT `s 32(3) -- the last day to object` `31 Oct 2025` EQUALS `28 Feb 2026`
-- Order: notice says expedited; government withdrew statement; notification day; objection lodged; lodged on; all
-- withdrawn; found attracts; found does not attract; today.
-- E1 no statement in the notice: negotiation.
#ASSERT `s 32 -- can the act go ahead without negotiating with us` FALSE FALSE `15 Jan 2026` FALSE `15 Jan 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `no: the notice did not say the act attracts the expedited procedure, so the negotiation parties must negotiate in good faith (s 31(1))`
-- E2 statement, no objection, today 1 June 2026 (after 15 May 2026): the act may be done.
#ASSERT `s 32 -- can the act go ahead without negotiating with us` TRUE FALSE `15 Jan 2026` FALSE `15 Jan 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `yes: no objection was lodged within 4 months after the notification day, so the Government party may do the act (s 32(2))`
-- E3 statement, no objection yet, today 15 May 2026 (the last day): may still object.
#ASSERT `s 32 -- can the act go ahead without negotiating with us` TRUE FALSE `15 Jan 2026` FALSE `15 Jan 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE `15 May 2026` EQUALS `not yet: you may still object, until the last day` `15 May 2026`
-- E4 objection lodged on the last day, not yet determined.
#ASSERT `s 32 -- can the act go ahead without negotiating with us` TRUE FALSE `15 Jan 2026` TRUE `15 May 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `not yet: your objection is lodged and the arbitral body has not yet determined it (s 32(4))`
-- E5 objection lodged a day late (16 May 2026): treated as no objection.
#ASSERT `s 32 -- can the act go ahead without negotiating with us` TRUE FALSE `15 Jan 2026` TRUE `16 May 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `yes: no objection was lodged within 4 months after the notification day, so the Government party may do the act (s 32(2))`
-- E6 objection upheld: the act does not attract the expedited procedure.
#ASSERT `s 32 -- can the act go ahead without negotiating with us` TRUE FALSE `15 Jan 2026` TRUE `1 Apr 2026` FALSE FALSE TRUE `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `no: the arbitral body determined the act does not attract the expedited procedure, so the negotiation parties must negotiate in good faith (ss 32(5), 31(1))`
-- E7 objection dismissed.
#ASSERT `s 32 -- can the act go ahead without negotiating with us` TRUE FALSE `15 Jan 2026` TRUE `1 Apr 2026` FALSE TRUE FALSE `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `yes: the arbitral body determined the act attracts the expedited procedure, so the Government party may do the act (s 32(4))`
-- E8 objection withdrawn before determination.
#ASSERT `s 32 -- can the act go ahead without negotiating with us` TRUE FALSE `15 Jan 2026` TRUE `1 Apr 2026` TRUE FALSE FALSE `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `yes: every objection was withdrawn, so the Government party may do the act (s 32(6))`
-- E9 the government withdrew its statement.
#ASSERT `s 32 -- can the act go ahead without negotiating with us` TRUE TRUE `15 Jan 2026` FALSE `15 Jan 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `no: the Government party withdrew its expedited procedure statement, so the negotiation parties must negotiate in good faith (ss 32(7), 31(1))`

§ `s 31(1C) -- party to the agreement`

-- 4 of 7 persons sign: a majority.
#ASSERT `s 31(1C) -- is our registered claimant a party to the agreement` 7 4 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: a majority of the persons who comprise the registered native title claimant are parties (s 31(1C)(a)); they must tell the others within a reasonable period (s 31(1D))`
-- 3 of 6: exactly half, not a majority.
#ASSERT `s 31(1C) -- is our registered claimant a party to the agreement` 6 3 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: fewer than a majority of the persons who comprise the registered native title claimant are parties (s 31(1C)(a), the text's no)`
-- 4 of 6: a majority.
#ASSERT `s 31(1C) -- is our registered claimant a party to the agreement` 6 4 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: a majority of the persons who comprise the registered native title claimant are parties (s 31(1C)(a)); they must tell the others within a reasonable period (s 31(1D))`
-- Conditions name who must sign; they all did, though only 2 of 7.
#ASSERT `s 31(1C) -- is our registered claimant a party to the agreement` 7 2 TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the persons the s 251BA conditions name are all parties to the agreement (s 31(1C)(b))`
-- Conditions name who must sign; 6 of 7 signed but not all named persons: no.
#ASSERT `s 31(1C) -- is our registered claimant a party to the agreement` 7 6 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: the s 251BA conditions name who must be parties, and not all of them are (s 31(1C)(b), the text's no)`

§ `s 35 -- applying for an arbitral body determination`

-- Notification day 15 January 2026: 6 months pass at the end of 15 July 2026; the first day is 16 July 2026.
#ASSERT `s 35(1) -- the first day to apply for a determination` `15 Jan 2026` EQUALS `16 Jul 2026`
-- Month end: 31 October 2025 plus 6 months is 30 April 2026; the first day is 1 May 2026.
#ASSERT `s 35(1) -- the first day to apply for a determination` `31 Oct 2025` EQUALS `1 May 2026`
#ASSERT `s 35 -- can we apply for an arbitral body determination` `15 Jan 2026` FALSE `16 Jul 2026` EQUALS `yes: at least 6 months have passed since the notification day and no agreement has been made (s 35(1)); you may withdraw the application, and keep negotiating, until a determination is made (s 35(2), (3))`
#ASSERT `s 35 -- can we apply for an arbitral body determination` `15 Jan 2026` FALSE `15 Jul 2026` EQUALS `not yet: 6 months have not passed since the notification day (s 35(1)(a), the text's no); the first day is` `16 Jul 2026`
#ASSERT `s 35 -- can we apply for an arbitral body determination` `15 Jan 2026` TRUE `16 Jul 2026` EQUALS `no: an agreement has been made about the act (s 35(1)(b), the text's no)`

§ `ss 36-38 -- what the arbitral body must do`

#ASSERT `ss 36-38 -- what the arbitral body must do on our application` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `it must make one of three determinations: the act must not be done, may be done, or may be done subject to conditions (s 38(1)); a condition cannot give you a share of profits, income or production (s 38(2)), though an agreement can (s 33(1))`
#ASSERT `ss 36-38 -- what the arbitral body must do on our application` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `it must not make a determination: an agreement has been made (s 37(a), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `ss 36-38 -- what the arbitral body must do on our application` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `it must not make a determination: the Minister has made a s 36A determination (s 37(b), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `ss 36-38 -- what the arbitral body must do on our application` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `it must not make the determination: another negotiation party did not negotiate in good faith (s 36(2), the text's no); a further application may be made under s 35`
#ASSERT `ss 36-38 -- what the arbitral body must do on our application` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `nothing: the application has been withdrawn (s 35(2), (3))`

§ `s 41 -- conditions as contract terms`

-- Order: subject to conditions; act done; negotiation party; in claim group of registered claimant party.
#ASSERT `s 41 -- can I enforce the conditions as contract terms` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: as a member of the claim group of a registered native title claimant that is a native title party, you are taken to be a negotiation party for this purpose (s 41(2)), so the conditions bind as contract terms (s 41(1))`
#ASSERT `s 41 -- can I enforce the conditions as contract terms` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the conditions have effect as terms of a contract among the negotiation parties, and you are one (s 41(1))`
#ASSERT `s 41 -- can I enforce the conditions as contract terms` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not yet: the conditions take effect as contract terms only if the act is done (s 41(1), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 41 -- can I enforce the conditions as contract terms` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: s 41(1) applies only to a determination or agreement that the act may be done subject to conditions (the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 41 -- can I enforce the conditions as contract terms` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not under s 41: you are neither a negotiation party nor a member of the claim group of a registered native title claimant that is a native title party (NOTHING-kind)`

§ `s 61 -- compensation application`

-- Order: body corporate holds; extinguished area inside determination; common law holders; applicant in group;
-- traditional process; authorised by it; authorised by agreed process.
#ASSERT `s 61 -- can we make a compensation application` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: our registered native title body corporate may apply, as it holds (or is agent for) the native title in the area (s 61(1), compensation item 1)`
#ASSERT `s 61 -- can we make a compensation application` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: our registered native title body corporate may apply on behalf of all who claim the compensation, for the extinguished area inside its determination (s 61(1), compensation item 1A)`
-- Extinguished area inside the determination, but the claimants are not the common law holders: not item 1A; no
-- authorised applicant either.
#ASSERT `s 61 -- can we make a compensation application` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: none of the persons s 61(1) lists for a compensation application is applying on these facts (the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 61 -- can we make a compensation application` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the person or persons our compensation claim group authorised may apply, and will jointly be the applicant (s 61(1), compensation item 2, s 61(2))`
#ASSERT `s 61 -- can we make a compensation application` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: none of the persons s 61(1) lists for a compensation application is applying on these facts (the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 61 -- can we make a compensation application` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: none of the persons s 61(1) lists for a compensation application is applying on these facts (the text's no)`

§ `ss 51, 51A -- compensation`

#ASSERT `s 51 -- which compensation rules apply` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `just terms for the effect on your native title (s 51(1)); as the act is a compulsory acquisition, the court may have regard to the principles in the acquisition law (s 51(2))`
#ASSERT `s 51 -- which compensation rules apply` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the court must apply the compensation principles of the law under which the similar compensable interest test is met, whether or not on just terms (s 51(3))`
#ASSERT `s 51 -- which compensation rules apply` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `just terms for the effect on your native title (s 51(1)); the court may have regard to the principles in the compulsory acquisition law of the Commonwealth or the State or Territory (s 51(4))`
#ASSERT `s 51 -- which compensation rules apply` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `just terms for the effect on your native title (s 51(1)); no other law's principles are named`
-- Cap: freehold value $1,200,000, no larger just terms figure: $1,200,000.
#ASSERT `s 51A -- the most compensation for extinguishing all native title` TRUE 1200000 0 EQUALS JUST 1200000
-- Just terms require $1,200,001: the cap gives way to s 53.
#ASSERT `s 51A -- the most compensation for extinguishing all native title` TRUE 1200000 1200001 EQUALS JUST 1200001
-- Just terms figure below the freehold value: the freehold value.
#ASSERT `s 51A -- the most compensation for extinguishing all native title` TRUE 1200000 900000 EQUALS JUST 1200000
-- Not all native title extinguished: s 51A sets no cap.
#ASSERT `s 51A -- the most compensation for extinguishing all native title` FALSE 1200000 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Order: asked; recommendation; complied; period ended.
#ASSERT `s 51(5)-(8) -- can our compensation be other than money` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `money only: compensation may only be the payment of money unless you ask for property, goods or services (s 51(5), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 51(5)-(8) -- can our compensation be other than money` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the court must consider your request, and may recommend property, goods or services instead of money (s 51(6))`
#ASSERT `s 51(5)-(8) -- can our compensation be other than money` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the recommendation was complied with: the property, goods or services are full compensation (s 51(8))`
#ASSERT `s 51(5)-(8) -- can our compensation be other than money` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the recommendation was not complied with: you may ask that the compensation be paid in money instead (s 51(7))`
#ASSERT `s 51(5)-(8) -- can our compensation be other than money` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `waiting: the period the recommendation specified has not ended (s 51(6)(b))`
